    {
      "id": "spgi-structure",
      "text": "S&P Global monetizes the same credit franchise three ways: Ratings (issuer-paid), S&P Dow Jones Indices (AUM-linked licensing, e.g. SPY), and Market Intelligence (IHS Markit) — all three appear as separate nodes.",
      "source": "S&P Global 10-K segment reporting"
    },
    {
      "id": "lseg-refinitiv",
      "text": "LSEG's $27B Refinitiv deal (2021) made data/analytics >70% of group revenue — LSEG is now primarily a data company that happens to own exchanges.",
      "source": "LSEG annual report"
    },
    {
      "id": "index-licensing",
      "text": "Index licensing is the highest-margin slice: MSCI and SPDJI collect basis points on trillions of indexed AUM (SPY tracks the S&P 500; iShares licenses MSCI indexes).",
